id: question-packets/node
title: "question packets node"
kind: mental-model-node
status: active
updated: 2026-08-27

purpose: >
  Hold simple intake contracts that let a person answer plain-language
  questions while an agent maps the answers into fuller .yawn templates.

holds:
  - basic question packet
  - relationship question packet
  - canonical nine-question orientation projection
  - turn close and replay packet

receives:
  - simple user answers
  - skipped answers
  - quotes, facts, inferences, desires, fears, and unknowns

produces:
  - draft-populated .yawn files
  - visible lacuna entries for missing answers
  - safer separation between observation, inference, boundary, move, and proof
  - stable orientation keys across adaptive wording order and medium

rules:
  - "Question packets are fill protocols, not competing templates."
  - "Skipped answers become lacuna.open_questions."
  - "Facts stay separate from inferences."
  - "Partner models stay hypothetical."
  - "Only authorized events update canonical materialized state."
  - "Only suitable evidence or proof upgrades empirical claims."
  - "Questions are projections over the ontology, not the ontology."
  - "Adaptive inquiry uses core/inquiry-selection.yawn and preserves question_key, exact_rendered_prompt, representation_medium, and answer_input_adapter provenance."

links:
  - questions/node.yawn
  - question-packets/basic.yawn
  - question-packets/relationship.yawn
  - question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  - question-packets/turn-close.yawn
  - core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  - templates/full.yawn
  - templates/relationship.yawn
  - examples/relationship-commitment-conversation.yawn

proof:
  source:
    - readme.yawn
    - templates/full.yawn
    - templates/relationship.yawn
    - question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
    - core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  status: draft-backed
